This wasn't changed in the latest posting.  There are 2 ways to take care of
this problem.

"log1p(x)" is equal to "log(1+x)".  You can just go through all the servers
that have that function in it ("grep log1p *.c") and change them all,
or you can add this function to "vars.h":


---------------------->8-->8---*Snip* *Snip*---8<--8<----------------------

double log1p(x)
double x;
{
	return(log(1+x));
}


---------------------->8-->8---*Snip* *Snip*---8<--8<----------------------

As "vars.h" is #included in most (I believe ALL) the files, log1p will get
defined throughout the programs.


